We can gather this field of concern as $\mathcal{Q}_{\mathrm{Bohm}}
=
\{\text{time},\ \text{space},\ \text{matter},\ \text{causality},\ \text{universality}\}.$ The notation $\mathcal{Q}_{\mathrm{Bohm}}$ is editorial. It names the cluster of questions that prepared Bohm to recognize something in Krishnamurti’s work. The point is not that Krishnamurti gave Bohm a physics equation. The point is that Bohm’s own discipline had already led him toward questions that were not merely technical.

