For Bohm’s physics-facing reference, we may write the cautious schematic $\text{observer}
\quad\longrightarrow\quad
\text{observed particle}.$ The arrow means involvement, effect, or disturbance. It is not a measurement operator and not a hidden derivation. It simply marks the fact that observation is not always external to what is observed.

