The movement is worth displaying because it prevents us from treating the observer/observed question as a one-time intellectual coincidence: $\text{reading}
\longrightarrow
\text{conversation}
\longrightarrow
\text{repeated meetings}
\longrightarrow
\text{shared work at Brockwood}.$ The point of this sequence is continuity. A conceptual recognition became a relationship of inquiry.

